        "effectiveDate": "2005-11-01",
        "isIndefinite": true
      },
      "status": "active",
      "statusHistory": [

      ],
      "referenceNumber": "CDe.008",
      "remarks": "Goma, with provincial committees in South Kivu, Kasai Occidental, Kasai\nOriental and Maniema Officially suspended all activities since 2008. In practice, as of\nJune 2011 TPD offices are open and involved in cases related to returns of IDPs,\ncommunity reconciliation initiatives, land conflict settlements, etc. The TPD President\nis Eugene Serufuli and Vice-President is Saverina Karomba. Important members include\nNorth Kivu provincial deputies Robert Seninga and Bertin Kirivita. INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities",
      "rawSourceData": {
        "@type": "RawSourceData",
        "sourceFormat": "xml",
        "sourceSpecificFields": {
          "un:dataId": "6908030",
          "un:versionNum": "1",
          "un:entityType": "entity"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://www.ammitto.org/entity/un/cde009",
      "@type": "OrganizationEntity",
      "entityType": "organization",
      "names": [
        {
          "@type": "NameVariant",
          "fullName": "UGANDA COMMERCIAL IMPEX (UCI) LTD",
          "script": "Latn",
          "isPrimary": true
        }
      ],
      "sourceReferences": [

      ],
      "linkedEntities": [

      ],
      "hasSanctionEntry": [
        "https://www.ammitto.org/entry/un/consolidated-list/cde009"
      ],
      "remarks": "Gold export company. (Directors Mr. Jamnadas V. LODHIA – known as\n“Chuni”- and his sons Mr. Kunal LODHIA and Jitendra J. LODHIA). In January 2011, Ugandan\nauthorities notified the Committee that following an exemption on its financial\nholdings, Emirates Gold repaid UCI’s debt to Crane Bank in Kampala, leading to final\nclosure of its accounts. The directors of UCI have remained involved in purchasing gold\nfrom eastern DRC. Uganda Commercial Impex (UCI) Ltd last filed a return in 2013 and was listed as “Inactive – status inactive” by the authorities of the Republic of Uganda.  INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Entities",
      "identifications": [

      ],
      "addresses": [
        {
