      ],
      "remarks": "Under house arrest in Kinshasa since March 2005 for FNI involvement in\nhuman rights abuses. Transferred to The Hague on 27 March 2011 to testify in the ICC\nGermain Katanga and Mathieu Ngudjolo trials. Applied for asylum in the Netherlands in\nMay 2011. In October 2012, a Dutch court denied his asylum claim. In July 2014, he was\ndeported from the Netherlands to DRC, where he was placed under arrest. INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Individuals",
      "birthInfo": [
