      "hasSanctionEntry": [
        "https://www.ammitto.org/entry/un/consolidated-list/cdi022"
      ],
      "remarks": "Former RCD-G General. Founder, National Congress for the People’s\nDefense, 2006; Senior Officer, Rally for Congolese Democracy-Goma (RCD-G), 1998-2006;\nOfficer Rwandan Patriotic Front (RPF), 1992-1998. Laurent Nkunda was arrested by Rwandan\nauthorities in Rwanda in January 2009 and replaced as the commander of the CNDP. Since\nthen, he has been under house arrest in Kigali, Rwanda. DRC Government’s request to\nextradite Nkunda for crimes committed in eastern DRC has been refused by Rwanda. In\n2010, Nkunda’s appeal for illegal detention was rejected by Rwandan court in Gisenyi,\nruling that the matter should be examined by a military court. Nkunda’s lawyers appealed\nwith the Rwandan Military Court. INTERPOL-UN Security Council Special Notice:https://www.interpol.int/en/How-we-work/Notices/View-UN-Notices-Individuals",
      "birthInfo": [
        {
          "@type": "BirthInfo",
          "date": "1967-02-06",
          "circa": false,
          "year": 1967,
          "city": "Rutshuru",
          "region": "North Kivu",
          "country": "Democratic Republic of the Congo"
        }
      ],
      "nationalities": [
        "Democratic Republic of the Congo"
      ],
      "gender": "Male",
